  "key_evidence": [
    "Why it matters: Latvia's published score was never measured. Its eight dimension values are byte-identical to those of the Czech Republic (rank 28), Lithuania (rank 31) and Slovenia (rank 33) - four neighbouring countries sharing one placeholder vector.",
    "Latvia launched a militarised border operation, \"Vilkatis\"/\"Werewolf\", on 11 August 2026, adding drones, helicopters, aircraft and troops. Border guards have prevented 9,521 entries this year. Latvia attributes the movement to Belarus and Russia; that instrumentalisation is NOT scored against Latvia.",
    "Amnesty International records that 2024 legal amendments gave border guards powers to \"prevent\" irregular entries, which in practice produce unlawful summary returns. B4 (Refusal Ethics) scores 2 of 5.",
    "In January the authorities opened criminal smuggling proceedings against two members of the NGO \"I Want to Help Refugees\" for assisting migrants at the border. A4 (Signal Amplification) scores 2 of 5.",
    "CALIBRATION CHECK: Poland, which faces the same Belarus border situation and has been individually assessed, sits at 42.2 Functional. Greece is 39.1, Croatia 40.6, Hungary 50.2. Latvia at 48.8 sits within the individually assessed European cohort; the seed value of 62.5 is the outlier."
